From: kevin03L <kevin03L@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btintel: do not report unsupported debug features as an error

Older Intel controllers (here 8087:0a2b, firmware 14-44.2021) have no "read supported features"
vendor command (0xfca6) and always answer Command Disallowed (status 0x0c, -EBUSY), also long
after setup. It only serves the optional debug events and device coredumps, and the driver goes
on without them, yet each boot logs

  Bluetooth: hci0: Reading supported features failed (-16)
  Bluetooth: hci0: Error reading debug features

Keep the error for every other status.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btintel.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btintel.c
@@ -1434,6 +1434,11 @@ static int btintel_read_debug_features(s
 	skb = __hci_cmd_sync(hdev, 0xfca6, sizeof(page_no), &page_no,
 			     HCI_INIT_TIMEOUT);
 	if (IS_ERR(skb)) {
+		/* Command Disallowed: no such command on older controllers */
+		if (PTR_ERR(skb) == -EBUSY) {
+			bt_dev_dbg(hdev, "Debug features not supported");
+			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+		}
 		bt_dev_err(hdev, "Reading supported features failed (%ld)",
 			   PTR_ERR(skb));
 		return PTR_ERR(skb);
@@ -1606,7 +1611,8 @@ static int btintel_register_devcoredump_
 
 	err = btintel_read_debug_features(hdev, &features);
 	if (err) {
-		bt_dev_info(hdev, "Error reading debug features");
+		if (err != -EOPNOTSUPP)
+			bt_dev_info(hdev, "Error reading debug features");
 		return err;
 	}
 
